{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-2540",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{5}+2 & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{x}{5}+2-2 & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\ \\frac{x}{5}+0 & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{6}{3} \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, multiplying both sides of the equation by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{5} & =-\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\cancel{5}\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\cancel{5}} & =5\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
